tournament_election v1.0.0 -- Demo
======================================================================

1. SIMPLE ELECTION (clear winner)
  Condorcet winner: Alice
  Transitivity:     1.000
  Copeland:         [('Alice', 2), ('Bob', 1), ('Carol', 0)]
  Methods agree:    True

2. CONDORCET PARADOX (no clear winner)
  Condorcet winner: None (none!)
  Condorcet cycles: 1
  Transitivity:     0.000
  Smith set:        {'Bob', 'Alice', 'Carol'}
  Copeland:         [('Bob', 1), ('Alice', 1), ('Carol', 1)]
  Schulze:          [('Alice', 0), ('Bob', 0), ('Carol', 0)]
  Paradoxical:      True

3. REALISTIC ELECTION (5 candidates)
  Voters:           100
  Condorcet winner: None
  Condorcet cycles: 2
  Transitivity:     0.800
  Smith set:        {'Centrist', 'Progressive', 'Conservative', 'Liberal'}
  Margin strength:  21.8

  Rankings comparison:
      Method                                                      Ranking
    copeland Centrist(3) > Liberal(3) > Progressive(2) > Conservative(2) > Populist(0)
     schulze Liberal(4) > Progressive(3) > Centrist(2) > Conservative(1) > Populist(0)
       borda Centrist(94.0) > Liberal(54.0) > Progressive(46.0) > Conservative(24.0) > Populist(0)
  Methods agree: False

4. TOURNAMENT STABILITY
  3 candidates, 50 random voters: stability=0, transitivity=1.000, cycles=0
  4 candidates, 50 random voters: stability=0, transitivity=1.000, cycles=0
  5 candidates, 50 random voters: stability=1, transitivity=0.800, cycles=2
